@Telford & Steve: My argument is that Trump is an "idiot", "disaster", "threat to world peace", "tweeted something un-presidential" etc etc - gig is getting stale. We get it. If that means "defending" him (something I did not do at all talking about the DNC/Clinton); it just shows how obsessed with Trump bashing BS/DM/detractor have become. 

Instead, I am arguing, why not report, reflect and provide opinion on the biggest news story of the week. Heck, BS, can still get in all his swipes at Trump.

Instead, I would suggest the silence, shows why the whole "fake news" meme is now mostly associated with the mainstream media. Why a plurality of Americans think the media make up stories on Trump. That the media will jump on every single scandal associated with Team Red, but when it comes to Team Blue - obfuscate,  delay and hand-wave. 

@Steve - The mysterious Republican has not been revealed and backed up with a name. The DNC/Clinton angle has...so what is the better claim for now?

